lantern-pr 1
# 66
#title Block a dropped file from navigating the editor webview
#url https://github.com/MobileReality/lantern/pull/66
#branch fix/editor-file-drop-guard
#base main
#opened 2026-11-18
#head 1e3ac519e3aa26500c054f6b63443d0efe4380ed
#describe what The editor webview now refuses to navigate to a local file, which is what an unhandled file drop did, and a notification tells the user to use the + button in the Claude Code panel.
#describe before A dropped image that the chat panel did not consume replaced the whole editor with that image.
#describe after The navigation is cancelled, the editor stays, and the notice appears at most once every few seconds.
#describe verified Typecheck is clean and the new tests pass. The cause is inferred from the code and was not reproduced in the running app.
~ src/main/main.ts
~ src/main/windows.ts
~ src/shared/lang/en/messages.json
~ test/webview-hardening.test.ts
#order src/main/windows.ts
#order src/main/main.ts
#order src/shared/lang/en/messages.json
#order test/webview-hardening.test.ts
#reason src/main/main.ts Attaches the guard to every webview guest and tells the user a dropped file was not attached.
#reason src/main/windows.ts Adds the guard the editor webview lacked, since the host window's will-navigate never sees guest navigations.
#reason src/shared/lang/en/messages.json Holds the notice text shown when a dropped file is stopped, as every user-facing string goes through msg().
#reason test/webview-hardening.test.ts Pins that a file navigation is blocked and reported once, and that editor addresses still navigate.
#story A dropped screenshot no longer replaces the editor
#step actor A Lantern user
#step action drops an image file onto
#file src/main/windows.ts
#step subject the Claude Code panel
#below actor The same user
#file src/main/main.ts
#below interaction is told the file was not attached and to use +
#file src/shared/lang/en/messages.json
#below consequence the editor turned into the image => the editor stays as it was
#file test/webview-hardening.test.ts
